  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given positive integers A,B,A, B,A,B, and KKK.\n\nFor a variable xxx with an initial value AAA, you need to achieve the target value BBB. In one operation, you can:\n\n\nEither change xxx to x+1x + 1x+1, or\nChange xxx to K⋅xK \\cdot xK⋅x.\nFind the **minimum** number of operations needed to go from x=Ax = Ax=A to x=Bx = Bx=B.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case contains three space-separated integers A,B,KA, B, KA,B,K — the initial and target values of the variable xxx and the constant.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line, the **minimum** number of operations needed to go from x=Ax = Ax=A to x=Bx = Bx=B.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1041 \\le T \\le 10^41≤T≤104",
      "1≤A&lt;B≤1091 \\le A \\lt B \\le 10^91≤A&lt;B≤109",
      "2≤K≤1092 \\le K \\le 10^92≤K≤109"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "4\n1 8 2\n3 8 2\n3 7 2\n1 1000000000 900000000",
        "output": "3\n2\n2\n100000001",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111 : We can use the second type of operation thrice to get A=1→2→4→8=BA = 1 \\rightarrow 2 \\rightarrow 4 \\rightarrow 8 = BA=1→2→4→8=B.\nTest case 222 : We can use the first type of operation to get x=4x = 4x=4 and then the second  operation to get x=2⋅4=8=Bx = 2\\cdot 4 = 8 = Bx=2⋅4=8=B.\nTest case 333 : Second operation and then the first operation yields 3→6→73 \\rightarrow 6 \\rightarrow 73→6→7."
      }
    ]
  },
